 i don't know that moses because  he goes for so many languages i don't  don't know that he achieves a  tremendously high level in in most of  them he may and some of them i just  don't know  uh  but his would have been an interesting  case because he doesn't come from a  multi-lingual environment like some of  the people they mentioned in the book  catalam is mentioned in the book and she  says something like  we learn grammar from language we don't  learn language from grammar which i  think is a very interesting quote so  there's a bunch of nuggets in the book  uh one of the things that i discovered  in reading the book is that chewing gum  is good for studying and so i looked it  up on the internet and what it is is  that if you're chewing you're creating  saliva and that sends insulin around  your body and increases the oxygen  supply to your brain and they figured  that you can even increase the  effectiveness of your studying by 20 by  chewing gum or chewing while you study  hey there's something  uh he talks about you know the  importance of the hippocampus this area  of your brain the importance of dopamine  in other words a sense of satisfaction  and achievement  that spurs you on to more activity it  made me think that of course dopamine  production has increased with exercise  and the exercise also makes your  hippocampus  uh more effective and the hippocampus is  where we kind of manage things in our  brain a little bit that i understand  so exercise is probably good for you too  so you want to run around chewing gum  maybe listen to an mp3 player um  do a lot of those things  i don't know  he sort of at one point he says the only  difference between these hyper glots as  he calls them and ordinary people is  that the hyper gloss are willing to  you know do things that are inherently  boring well i certainly disagree with  that comment because  i don't find it boring i would find  making little sailboats to put in  bottles boring  uh but you know i get 