out historical  polyglots in europe americans you know  all kinds he's done even did a survey of  polyglots as to what they felt was the  most important element and of course  that generally was  the attitude and and liking the activity  which is not surprising  so  uh you might want to read it i think  it's a good read it has a lot of useful  information  it's written uh in a very sort of uh  entertaining  modest  sort of discovering let's discover  something together kind of way  and there's a lot of useful  little uh tidbits of information  personally i came away more convinced  than ever that uh  you know someone who you know  the first language you learn takes a  long time because you haven't done it  before  if you then want to do another one it  goes much more quickly because you're  more confident you know how to do it  um  now if you learn spanish you can learn  the other romance languages pretty  easily i mean i'm having a lot easier  time with czech than i had with russian  uh having learned chinese i had half the  vocabulary in japanese so  given the fact that our skills get  better and our brain probably gets  more fit in terms of language learning  and that  all languages have related languages so  that once you learn  russian you can learn czech and polish  and ukrainian  uh in less time than you spend on the  first language it's not impossible that  people who dedicated themselves who had  all the time in the world could learn 20  30 languages i don't find that so  strange no more strange than someone who  plays 10 musical instruments uh it's a  matter of what you like to do  um  and and if that's your job so language  learning still comes down to the basics  your attitude your motivation you you  like it you're determined to do it blah  blah blah attitude  two time if you can send eight ten hours  a day of learning languages you can rack  up a lot of languages and the third one  is this whole  idea of noticing identifying patterns  getting and we get better at that the  more we listen the more we read the more  we study languages we get better doing  those things so  as i always say attitude time on task  and developing the ability to notice  what's happening  so there you go babel no more an  interesting read for people who are  interested in learning languages bye for  now

